A||||6||Homicidal||Brake Dust Covers?||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||08-30-2000||06:54 PM||||My rims get WAY too dirty TOO fast from the brake dust!  Is there anywhere to prevent this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sillhouette.com||08-30-2000||08:03 PM||||Get yourself some crossed drilled rotors somehow they create ventilation that carries brake dust away from the rims.... On my car anyways..<P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||08-30-2000||08:04 PM||||I used some dust covers for a while.  They kept the dust off the lace wheels, but rubbed the brake calipers.  So every wheel revolution they squeaked.  When the brakes were changed the dust covers  were worn through and there wasn't enough clearence for them to go back.  Now it just alot of wheel cleaning.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Boomtastic||08-30-2000||08:49 PM||||You can also try switching brake pad compounds too maybe something a little harder, like Carbon Metallics, Kevlars, etc. I haven't had that much of a dust problem since I got away from the "cheap" pads.||||reg||3
Z||000004||Shiner||08-30-2000||11:22 PM||||*** Cliff, when are you going to let us erase our gosh darn double posts?!?!**<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by Shiner (edited 08-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shiner||08-30-2000||11:22 PM||||Homicidal,<BR> Ever notice how German cars always have lots of front brake dust on the rims?  It's because of a softer pad material.  The tradeoff is that they will stop the car quicker than those $10 full metallic brake pads with the lifetime warranty you will find at Autozone.  <P> Sillhouette,<BR> Yeah, cross drilled rotors look trick, but they do NOTHING more on the street for braking distance or fade (over a slotted rotor) except crack and wear quicker.<P>------------------<BR>Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)<BR>"Stupidity should hurt"||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sillhouette.com||08-31-2000||06:06 AM||||Wow that is interesting.   <P>I have cross drilled on both my GTP and Fiero.  I had the cross drilled on my Wbody for two years.  Did not need to change the pads yet and I also pull a 2000 lbs of Sea Doo with it on the highway.  If anyone know anything about Wbodies you should know that the brakes are the worst with a lot of brake fade from the factory.  The cross drilled fixed them with ability to lock tyres on a 17" rims.  I also know that now my rims are a whole lot cleaner than before when I spent close to 15 minutes cleaning the front two rims alone.  These are the facts that I have experienced and that is why cross drilled are better.  Do you have any proof that cross drilled are not better than straight rotors?  Have you done distance trials?<P>Later||||reg||1
